laurel 2015: per-CPU GIC redistributor init with read-back (pe_fiq.c laurel_gicr_setup) and a panel report at STARTUP(LOCKDOWN). Boot 2026-11-01 02:57 on the UEFI path (Mu-Silicium -> UniXNU -> DarwinBoot, boot CPU Silver 0x0): the 2013 self-check read GICR ISENABLER0 bit 19 = 0 after pe_init_fiq had written it, CNTV_CTL ISTATUS=1, ICC/GICD fine: no timer tick reached the boot CPU, every thread starved (PE_lockdown_iokit, ud_thread, bsd_init). The setup now: find_gicr_pe_base prefers a frame whose TYPER is not 0 (a dead frame reads 0 and matches MPIDR 0x0); disable + deactivate + clear pending SGIs/PPIs, IGROUPR0 = ~0, IGRPMODR0 = 0, priority 0xA0, ISENABLER0 = vtimer 19 | ptimer 18 | IPI SGI 1; read back; on failure retry once after a GIC-600 GICR_PWRR power-on attempt. The boot CPU's record goes to the panel as 'LAUREL GIC: on|off: boot cpu mpidr=.. gicr frame N TYPER IIDR PWRR ISENABLER0 (was, want, try)' + a second line (IGROUPR0 IGRPMODR0 ISPENDR0 ISACTIVER0 ICFGR1 prio16 WAKER GICD_CTLR); secondaries kprintf one line into the ring. The 2013 USB check moves to RANK_SECOND and prints its GIC state on a second line (a 260-byte line was cut at the 256-byte console buffer). Harmless on the shim path (same writes as before plus the clears).
